## Hard rules (every change must satisfy)

1. **Multi-tenant scope.** Every Prisma read/write that touches workspace data MUST be scoped by `workspaceId`. Never query `Lead`, `AgentRun`, `SemanticMemory`, `WebsiteMockup`, `TeamTodo`, `WatchlistItem`, etc. without it. Cross-tenant leak = highest-severity bug class. Use `requireUser()` from `@/lib/auth` to get the active `workspaceId`.
2. **No `apiVersion` pin on Stripe.** SDK uses its compiled-against version (see `src/lib/stripe.ts`). Pinning broke types in v22.
3. **No top-level `env` block in `next.config.mjs`.** Anything declared there leaks to the client bundle. Read server secrets via `process.env` in server code only.
4. **`typescript.ignoreBuildErrors` stays `false`.** Fix type errors instead of bypassing.
5. **Generated client lives at `@/generated/prisma/client`** (custom `output` in schema). Don't import from `@prisma/client` in app code.
6. **Prisma engine + pg are `serverExternalPackages`.** Don't try to bundle them.

## Where to look first

| Need | Read first |
|---|---|
| New API route | `src/lib/auth.ts` (`requireUser`, `withAuth`), an existing route in same area |
| New AI worker | `src/lib/agent-workers/types.ts`, `registry.ts`, `quota.ts`, `execute.ts` |
| Memory read/write | `src/lib/ai-core/memory.ts` (NEVER touch `prisma.semanticMemory.*` directly) |
| Trigger AI work | `src/lib/ai-core/events.ts` → `emit(event, payload)` |
| New chain / DAG | `src/lib/ai-core/chains.ts`, `orchestrator.ts`, `planner.ts` |
| New BullMQ worker | `src/workers/index.ts`, an existing worker file |
| Plan limits | `src/lib/plans.ts`, `src/lib/agent-workers/quota.ts` |
| Stripe webhook | `src/app/api/billing/webhook/route.ts`, idempotency via `StripeEventLog` |
| DB schema | `prisma/schema.prisma` (~700 lines; grep first before reading whole) |
| Brand colors / tokens | `src/app/globals.css` (CSS vars: `--revint-*`, `--cine-*`, `--system-*`) |

## Commands you may need

```bash
npm run dev                # next dev --webpack
npm run workers            # tsx src/workers/index.ts (BullMQ supervisor)
npm run db:push            # prisma db push (dev — no migration history)
npm run db:generate        # prisma generate after schema edits
npm run test               # vitest run (unit)
npm run test:integration   # vitest with integration config
npm run lint               # eslint .
```

## Things NOT to do

- Don't add new BullMQ queues; extend AI Core (`src/lib/ai-core/`) or use `agent-runs` queue.
- Don't add new Gemini-calling endpoints outside `src/lib/agent-workers/` or `src/lib/ai-core/router.ts`.
- Don't read `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` — those docs are NOT bundled in this install. For Next.js 16 specifics, see the `nextjs-16.mdc` rule (auto-loaded for app/middleware/config files).
- Don't write to `Lead`, `AgentRun`, etc. without `workspaceId` in the where clause / data.
- Don't import from `@prisma/client`; use `@/generated/prisma/client`.
